{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>A wild ass of a man.</b> A trader who goes with his merchandise far away to a place where they do not know him, as it is said: 'a caravan of Ishmaelites coming from Gilead.' And 'a wild ass of a man' in Old French means a stranger. A stranger is called פרא, as you say: 'and a wild ass's colt is born a man' (Job 11:12)." "<b>His hand against all.</b> Against every kind of merchandise." "<b>And everyone's hand against him.</b> Through the give-and-take of trade in merchandise." "<b>And before all his brothers he shall dwell.</b> His holdings shall spread among all his brothers because of his abundant wealth. Another interpretation: 'and he shall be a wild ass of a man' — like the wild creature called gars in Old French. <b>His hand against all</b> — that he will defeat everyone, and afterward, 'and everyone's hand against him' — that they will defeat him in the end."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "פרא here is connected both to the trade/stranger sense and to the Job verse; the Old French gloss is not given in the Hebrew text and must be inferred.", 3 "גרא״ז appears to be an Old French gloss; exact Old French word uncertain from the transliteration."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:27.989744470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}